I walk over towards the cash register with my new jacket.
On the way, I see a really nice shirt.
It is light blue and made of soft cotton.
I actually need a new shirt for the office.
I take the shirt down from the hanger.
I look over at the fitting rooms.
There are a lot of people in the store today.
The line for the fitting rooms is very long.
I do not want to wait for a long time.
Therefore, I decide that I will not try it on first.
I usually wear size medium.
I check the shirt's size.
However, I think that it looks a little small.
But a bigger size is probably too big.
And a smaller size will definitely be too tight.
So I just take my normal size.
I put the shirt over my arm together with the jacket.
I hope the shirt fits at home.
